WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.220
Peer review relies entirely on an
architecture of trust.

2
00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:07.140
Unauthorized delegation transforms that
architecture into an engine for

3
00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:12.360
academic sabotage. Beyond peer review
failures, compromised research design

4
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.760
also degrades the scientific record,
particularly through post hoc data

5
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:21.760
manipulation. A prime example is harking,
hypothesizing after the results are

6
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.520
known, while failing to disclose the
timeline.

7
00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:28.040
This vector loop illustrates the standard
scientific method.

8
00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.180
Harking reverses that direction.

9
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:34.800
The results aggressively override the
initial hypothesis to match the data,

10
00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:36.980
creating a false narrative of success.

11
00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:41.400
As this corrupted logic spreads, it
misleads future researchers.

12
00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:45.520
A parallel danger occurs when researchers
insufficiently report the inherent

13
00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:48.480
study flaws or limitations within their
datasets.

14
00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:51.960
This lack of transparency often results in
spin.

15
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.120
The deliberate linguistic or statistical
inflation of results to artificially

16
00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:01.240
manufacture significance. Post-hoc data
manipulation and spin strip research

17
00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:05.580
of its predictive value, rendering the
underlying science practically useless.

18
00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:10.500
Modern research ethics demand systemic,
preventative solutions to these

19
00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:14.600
vulnerabilities, rather than relying on
after-the-fact corrections.

20
00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:18.940
Practices like the prospective
registration of clinical trials and the

21
00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:23.280
preregistration of animal study protocols
lock in experimental parameters

22
00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:28.400
early. Statistical preregistration secures
the methodology before any data

23
00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:31.512
collection begins, neutralizing the threat
of harking.
